WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:15.907
Katie and Joy raced their bikes down Blackberry Road.

2
00:00:15.908 --> 00:00:18.691
"We'll be late!" Joy shouted.

3
00:00:18.692 --> 00:00:21.889
"All because you couldn't get out of bed!"

4
00:00:21.890 --> 00:00:27.518
"It's summer!" Katie called back. "We're allowed to sleep late!"

5
00:00:27.519 --> 00:00:31.072
"Not today!" Joy reminded her.

6
00:00:31.073 --> 00:00:35.966
The twins turned left on County Road and sped toward town.

7
00:00:35.967 --> 00:00:39.280
Luke was running out of his front door.

8
00:00:39.281 --> 00:00:41.738
"Hurry, Luke!" Joy called.

9
00:00:41.739 --> 00:00:46.390
The girls flew past Aunt Sally's house and down Main Street.

10
00:00:46.391 --> 00:00:50.865
A crowd of boys and girls had gathered at the town park.

11
00:00:50.866 --> 00:00:53.583
A banner flapped between two trees.

12
00:00:53.584 --> 00:00:57.466
It said "WILLOW CREEK DAY CAMP."

13
00:00:57.467 --> 00:00:59.725
"Hey!" yelled Laura.

14
00:00:59.726 --> 00:01:03.393
She ran across the grass to Katie and Joy.

15
00:01:03.394 --> 00:01:05.834
"You're here!"

16
00:01:05.835 --> 00:01:09.552
"Yep," said Katie. "This better be fun."

17
00:01:09.553 --> 00:01:11.971
She looked around the park.

18
00:01:11.972 --> 00:01:14.717
"There's Carlos!" said Joy.

19
00:01:14.718 --> 00:01:18.956
Carlos and his little brother Manny were playing kickball.

20
00:01:18.957 --> 00:01:23.552
"Emily's here too," said Laura. "And AJ!"

21
00:01:23.553 --> 00:01:26.123
Emily Morgan was ten years old.

22
00:01:26.124 --> 00:01:29.949
Her brother AJ had just finished kindergarten.

23
00:01:29.950 --> 00:01:33.922
Luke's bike screeched to a stop beside the girls.

24
00:01:33.923 --> 00:01:38.253
Before they could say hello, they heard a loud whistle.

25
00:01:38.254 --> 00:01:42.982
"It's Mrs. Penkov," said Luke, hopping off his bike.

26
00:01:42.983 --> 00:01:47.214
Mrs. Penkov taught science at the high school.

27
00:01:47.215 --> 00:01:50.610
"Welcome to day camp! Come in, come in!"

28
00:01:50.611 --> 00:01:55.110
she shouted, marching the kids into the community center.

29
00:01:55.111 --> 00:01:58.463
"Are you the teacher?" asked Katie.

30
00:01:58.464 --> 00:02:02.370
"This isn't school!" Mrs. Penkov laughed.

31
00:02:02.371 --> 00:02:05.443
"I'm your day camp leader!"

32
00:02:05.444 --> 00:02:07.015
Katie looked around.

33
00:02:07.016 --> 00:02:13.950
She saw tables, chairs, bookshelves, computers, a whiteboard, and a map.

34
00:02:13.951 --> 00:02:17.642
"It looks like school," she said.

35
00:02:17.643 --> 00:02:22.699
"Day camp is two weeks of fun!" said Mrs. Penkov.

36
00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:25.737
"We'll play! We'll make friends! And . . ."

37
00:02:25.738 --> 00:02:28.070
She pointed to the map.

38
00:02:28.071 --> 00:02:30.302
"We'll explore our community.

39
00:02:30.303 --> 00:02:33.550
This is a special year for our town.

40
00:02:33.551 --> 00:02:39.579
In two weeks, it will be Willow Creek's one hundred fiftieth birthday!

41
00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:43.620
And all of you will get to be in the birthday parade!"

42
00:02:43.621 --> 00:02:49.195
Mrs. Penkov passed out little houses and buildings cut from colored paper.

43
00:02:49.196 --> 00:02:55.306
"Let's pin our houses to the map and show everyone where we live," she said.

44
00:02:55.307 --> 00:02:57.662
"I live here on Walnut Street."

45
00:02:57.663 --> 00:03:00.688
She pinned a house to the map.

46
00:03:00.689 --> 00:03:06.390
Carlos, Manny, Luke, and Laura pinned their houses on County Road.

47
00:03:06.391 --> 00:03:10.475
Emily and AJ put theirs on Blackberry Road.

48
00:03:10.476 --> 00:03:14.590
The other kids pinned their houses on the map too.

49
00:03:14.591 --> 00:03:19.493
Together they pinned the stores and town buildings to the map.

50
00:03:19.494 --> 00:03:25.511
"These are the places where people live and work in Willow Creek," said Mrs. Penkov.

51
00:03:25.512 --> 00:03:27.314
"This is our community!"

52
00:03:27.315 --> 00:03:29.088
She clapped her hands.

53
00:03:29.089 --> 00:03:32.417
The boys and girls clapped and cheered too.

54
00:03:32.418 --> 00:03:36.138
"Attention, campers!" said Mrs. Penkov.

55
00:03:36.139 --> 00:03:38.532
Everyone became quiet.

56
00:03:38.533 --> 00:03:41.345
"Now I have a special project for you.

57
00:03:41.346 --> 00:03:44.805
It's called a scavenger hunt."

58
00:03:44.806 --> 00:03:48.280
"What's that?" asked Manny.

59
00:03:48.281 --> 00:03:51.931
"Let me tell you how it works," said Mrs. Penkov.

60
00:03:51.932 --> 00:03:56.216
"First, we need to split into five teams."

61
00:03:56.217 --> 00:04:00.418
Katie and Luke were on a team with Emily and AJ.

62
00:04:00.419 --> 00:04:05.649
"Let's call our team the Earthworms," said Luke.

63
00:04:05.650 --> 00:04:08.623
Joy and Laura were with Carlos and Manny.

64
00:04:08.624 --> 00:04:12.601
"We'll be the Tornadoes," said Carlos.

65
00:04:12.602 --> 00:04:15.868
"Excellent!" said Mrs. Penkov.

66
00:04:15.869 --> 00:04:22.278
"Now I'll give each team a list of things to search for right here in Willow Creek!"

67
00:04:22.279 --> 00:04:27.191
"A yard sale announcement," said Luke, reading off the list.

68
00:04:27.192 --> 00:04:30.916
"A campaign button," read Laura.

69
00:04:30.917 --> 00:04:35.205
"A calendar of community events," read Joy.

70
00:04:35.206 --> 00:04:41.825
"Each thing you find will teach you something about our community," said Mrs. Penkov.

71
00:04:41.826 --> 00:04:45.482
"This looks hard," said Manny.

72
00:04:45.483 --> 00:04:49.479
"This looks like homework," said Katie.

73
00:04:49.480 --> 00:04:55.084
"Did I tell you?" cried Mrs. Penkov. "It's a contest!

74
00:04:55.085 --> 00:04:59.622
The team that finds the most things wins a prize."

75
00:04:59.623 --> 00:05:03.685
"I love prizes!" said Katie.

76
00:05:03.686 --> 00:05:07.754
Mrs. Penkov gave each team a shopping bag.

77
00:05:07.755 --> 00:05:13.165
"Keep everything you find in here," she said. "Happy hunting!

78
00:05:13.166 --> 00:05:14.600
See you on Wednesday.

79
00:05:14.601 --> 00:05:19.860
We'll be making parade hats and crowns!"
